mposable, and discoverable: users can write or fill orders without a privileged batcher, contracts publish clear datum/redeemer schemas, and orders can be found through on-chain mechanisms such as CIP-89 beacon tokens, deterministic addresses, or other tagging methods.\n\nDano Finance will support the DeFi Kernel adoption by improving the public **defikernel.org** platform and registry so any Cardano…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\nDano Finance and fallen-icarus are well suited to deliver this work because we are already building and operating Cardano DeFi infrastructure that follows the same principles the DeFi Kernel is designed to standardize: deterministic execution, composability, permissionless settlement, discoverability, and security-aware smart contract design.\n\nDano Finance currently has approximately **USD 18M** **in TVL** and more than **10,000 on-chain transactions**, showing practical experience in the KPI categories this proposal is designed to improve: TVL, users, protocol activity, and liquidity growth.…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**No competing proposals in this batch**\nNo other 2026 proposal targets the same use case (relationships.competes_with is empty).\n\nAre other proposals in this same round targeting the same use case? If two teams are both asking for treasury funding to build the same thing, a DRep should usually pick at most one — splitting the budget across competitors normally means both deliver less. This is the proposal's own competes_with declaration.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record c…47:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"no-competing-proposals\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"chi