ydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69fdc9b261c4f060e2fef6c9\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nThis proposal requests **3,300,000 ADA** for Dano Finance to accelerate the **DeFi Kernel** as an open standard for shared liquidity, on-chain financial intents, and global order-book coordination on Cardano.\n\nCardano DeFi is still fragmented. DEXs, lending protocols, options protocols, marketplaces, and future synthetic asset systems often operate as separate liquidity silos. The DeFi Kernel addresses this by defining a common standard where compatible smart contracts are permissionless, composable, and discoverable: users can write or fill orders without a privileged batcher, contracts publish clear datum/redeemer schemas, and orders can be found through on-chain mechanisms such as CIP-89 beacon tokens, deterministic addresses, or other tagging methods.\n\nDano Finance will support the DeFi Kernel adoption by improving the public **defikernel.org** platform and registry so any Cardano…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\nDano Finance and fallen-icarus are well suited to deliver this work because we are already building and operating Cardano DeFi infrastructure that follows the same principles the DeFi Kernel is designed to standardize: deterministic execution, composability, permissionless settlement, discoverability, and security-aware smart contract design.\n\nDano Finance currently has approximately **USD 18M** **in TVL** and more than **10,000 on-chain transactions**, showing practical experience in the KPI categories this proposal is designed to improve: TVL, users, protocol activity, and liquidity growth.…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**No incumbent is already delivering**\nNo existing project or team has already shipped this. Even if not flagged as a strict duplicate, funding this would not re-do work others have done or are funded to do.\n\nEven if not flagged as a strict duplicate, is an existing project or team already delivering this work? Passing means there's no incumbent — or the proposer has a credible argument for why their version is meaningfully different. Failing means funding this proposal would be re-doing work others have done or are already funded to do.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages,…48:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"incumbent-not-already-delivering\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"No incumbent is already delivering\"}]"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,",[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"label\":\"No incumbent is already delivering\",\"body\":\"Even if not flagged as a strict duplicate, is an existing project or team already delivering this work? Passing means there's no incumbent — or the proposer has a credible argument for why their version is meaningfully different. Failing means funding this proposal would be re-doing work others have done or are already funded to do.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"No existing project or team has already shipped this. Even if not flagged as a strict duplicate, funding this would not re-do work others have done or are funded to do.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$6b\"}]}],\"$L6c\"]}],\"$L6d\",\"$L6e\",\"$L6f\"]}]\n70:Tdbc,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before a