and orders can be found through on-chain mechanisms such as CIP-89 beacon tokens, deterministic addresses, or other tagging methods.\n\nDano Finance will support the DeFi Kernel adoption by improving the public **defikernel.org** platform and registry so any Cardano…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\nDano Finance and fallen-icarus are well suited to deliver this work because we are already building and operating Cardano DeFi infrastructure that follows the same principles the DeFi Kernel is designed to standardize: deterministic execution, composability, permissionless settlement, discoverability, and security-aware smart contract design.\n\nDano Finance currently has approximately **USD 18M** **in TVL** and more than **10,000 on-chain transactions**, showing practical experience in the KPI categories this proposal is designed to improve: TVL, users, protocol activity, and liquidity growth.…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**USD peg is not aggressive**\nPeg is conservative or neutral vs market — not requesting more ADA than spot would imply.\n\nProposals often denominate in USD at a chosen ADA price. If that peg is significantly below current market, the proposer is asking for more ADA than the same USD cost would actually require — an implicit overage. Conservative (at or above market) and neutral (within 5%) pegs are fine; aggressive pegs (more than 5% below market) are flagged.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the prop…50:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"usd-peg-not-aggressive\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font