rders without a privileged batcher, contracts publish clear…\n\nFull proposal JSON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69fdc9b261c4f060e2fef6c9\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nThis proposal requests **3,300,000 ADA** for Dano Finance to accelerate the **DeFi Kernel** as an open standard for shared liquidity, on-chain financial intents, and global order-book coordination on Cardano.\n\nCardano DeFi is still fragmented. DEXs, lending protocols, options protocols, marketplaces, and future synthetic asset systems often operate as separate liquidity silos. The DeFi Kernel addresses this by defining a common standard where compatible smart contracts are permissionless, composable, and discoverable: users can write or fill orders without a privileged batcher, contracts publish clear datum/redeemer schemas, and orders can be found through on-chain mechanisms such as CIP-89 beacon tokens, deterministic addresses, or other tagging methods.\n\nDano Finance will support the DeFi Kernel adoption by improving the public **defikernel.org** platform and registry so any Cardano…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\nDano Finance and fallen-icarus are well suited to deliver this work because we are already building and operating Cardano DeFi infrastructure that follows the same principles the DeFi Kernel is designed to standardize: deterministic execution, composability, permissionless settlement, discoverability, and security-aware smart contract design.\n\nDano Finance currently has approximately **USD 18M** **in TVL** and more than **10,000 on-chain transactions**, showing practical experience in the KPI categories this proposal is designed to improve: TVL, users, protocol activity, and liquidity growth.…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Measurable on-chain KPIs**\nProposal commits to specific, verifiable on-chain outcomes -- transactions, unique wallets, mainnet deployments, TVL -- not just GitHub commits or off-chain deliverables.\n\nJudgment call: does the proposal commit to specific on-chain KPIs that anyone can verify directly from the chain? Strong looks like 'X mainnet transactions per month, Y unique wallets, Z dApps integrated, all queryable via blockfrost or db-sync'. Weak looks like 'increase Cardano adoption', 'community growth', 'GitHub stars', or any metric the proposer themselves controls. On-chain metrics are tamper-proof and let the community measure delivery against the actual ledger, not the proposer's self-reported numbers.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this …58:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"measurable-onchain-kpis\",{\"className\":\"bo"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"rder-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Measurable on-chain KPIs\"}],[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"label\":\"Measurable on-chain KPIs\",\"body\":\"Judgment call: does the proposal commit to specific on-chain KPIs that anyone can verify directly from the chain? Strong looks like 'X mainnet transactions per month, Y unique wallets, Z dApps integrated, all queryable via blockfrost or db-sync'. Weak looks like 'increase Cardano adoption', 'community growth', 'GitHub stars', or any metric the proposer themselves controls. On-chain metrics are tamper-proof and let the community measure delivery against the actual ledger, not the proposer's self-reported numbers.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Proposal commits to specific, verifiable on-chain outcomes -- transactions, unique wallets, mainnet deployments, TVL -- not just GitHub commits or off-chain deliverables.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[